{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
# {{ theme.name }} fzf Theme

{% if adapter.mirror %}{%- set slug = theme.repository | replace(from="https://github.com/", to="") -%}
{%- set repo = adapter.mirror | split(pat="/") | last -%}
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This repository is a read-only mirror.
> Issues, pull requests, and stars should go to [{{ slug }}]({{ theme.repository }}).

{% endif -%}
fzf themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

### Manual

{% if adapter.mirror -%}
Clone the repository and source the theme file in your `.bashrc` or `.zshrc`:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ adapter.mirror }}.git
source /path/to/{{ repo }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.sh
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ repo }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.sh
```
{% endfor %}
### zinit

```zsh
zinit light-mode for \
  pick"{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.sh" \
  {{ adapter.mirror }}
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```zsh
zinit light-mode for \
  pick"{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.sh" \
  {{ adapter.mirror }}
```
{% endfor %}
### sheldon

Add to your `~/.config/sheldon/plugins.toml`:

```toml
[plugins.{{ repo }}]
github = "{{ adapter.mirror }}"
use = ["{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.sh"]
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```toml
[plugins.{{ repo }}]
github = "{{ adapter.mirror }}"
use = ["{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.sh"]
```
{% endfor %}
### oh-my-zsh

Clone as a custom plugin:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ adapter.mirror }} ${ZSH_CUSTOM:-~/.oh-my-zsh/custom}/plugins/{{ repo }}
```

Then add to your `.zshrc`:

```zsh
plugins=(... {{ repo }})
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
To use {{ v.variant.id }} variant, set before loading oh-my-zsh:

```zsh
export {{ theme.id | upper }}_VARIANT={{ v.variant.id }}
```
{% endfor %}
### antigen

```zsh
antigen bundle {{ adapter.mirror }}
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
To use {{ v.variant.id }} variant, set before loading:

```zsh
export {{ theme.id | upper }}_VARIANT={{ v.variant.id }}
```
{% endfor %}
{% else -%}
Source the theme file in your `.bashrc` or `.zshrc`:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.sh
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
source /path/to/{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.sh
```
{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
